WEBVTT

00:06:27.413 --> 00:06:30.746
And then I'm encouraged to message my friend,

00:06:30.746 --> 00:06:32.579
but here's the critical difference.

00:06:32.579 --> 00:06:36.246
I'm provided specific suggested language

00:06:36.246 --> 00:06:38.579
that helps me communicate to Laura

00:06:38.579 --> 00:06:40.496
how the photo makes me feel.

00:06:40.496 --> 00:06:43.538
Now the team found that this relatively small change

00:06:43.538 --> 00:06:45.204
had a huge impact.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:47.621
Before, only 20 percent of people

00:06:47.621 --> 00:06:48.788
were sending the message,

00:06:48.788 --> 00:06:50.829
and now 60 percent were,

00:06:50.829 --> 00:06:52.454
and surveys showed that people

00:06:52.454 --> 00:06:54.413
on both sides of the conversation

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:56.038
felt better as a result.

00:06:56.038 --> 00:06:57.704
That same survey showed

00:06:57.704 --> 00:07:00.038
that 90 percent of your friends